+```text
+DOTNET_ROOT=/opt/dotnet-10 DOTNET_ROOT_X64=/opt/dotnet-10 \
+  src/lancer/bin/Release/net10.0/lancer --sdl-gpu-pbr-spotlight-smoke
+```
+
+The probe drew the same synthetic front-facing triangle twice with the
+production PBR shader. The aligned point spotlight produced a readback luma of
+241; reversing its direction put the sample outside the cone and produced luma
+0. Both samples were opaque. The run used SDL_GPU/Vulkan on Mesa Intel Haswell;
+Mesa warned that Haswell Vulkan support is incomplete.
+
+![Production PBR spotlight in-cone and out-of-cone comparison](spotlight-comparison.png)
+
+This demonstrates the PBR spotlight cone response on this driver. It does not
+validate retail light data, material binding in a Freelancer scene, or general
+PBR color calibration. The probe now uploads the reflected 176-byte PBR block,
+including `AmbientScale` at byte 112. The standard synthetic PBR readback is
+`(200, 150, 0, 255)` and its shadowed sample is `(0, 0, 0, 255)`; the standard
+PBR color and shadow checks pass. The aligned and reversed spotlight samples
+remain luma 241 and 0. Mesa reports incomplete Haswell Vulkan support.
+
+The probe writes the complete compare frame from the same Release run to
+[`spotlight-comparison.ppm`](spotlight-comparison.ppm) and the PNG above. It
+validates the shader and synthetic uniform payload, not the C# `BasicMaterial`
+uniform layout or a real Freelancer scene. The production material layout is
+checked separately by the PBR uniform-layout fix in patch 2490.
